Green butadiene, also known as bio-based butadiene, is produced from renewable feedstocks such as sugar cane, corn, and other biomass sources. It offers an alternative to conventional petroleum-derived butadiene, which is widely used in synthetic rubber, thermoplastic elastomers, and other chemical products. Advances in fermentation and bio-based conversion technologies are supporting efforts to scale production and improve commercial viability.

